<Base
  lang="en"
  page="status"
  eyebrow="Features and limits"
  title="Current implementation"
  description="Available features, the checks applied and what remains to be completed."
>
  <p class="lede">
    Lanternina is a prototype used in one home. Its activity path includes approval, printing, page reading and continuation. Some functions remain incomplete, and installation in other homes still needs to be tried.
  </p>

  <h2>Available features</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      The panel lets the parent prepare ideas, approve activities and choose preferences and hours.
    </li>
    <li>
      The house shows instructions on displays, prints pages and starts a scan when a button is pressed.
    </li>
    <li>
      The system generates activities and pages, reads added marks and prepares continuations. The household clock manages help and the start of the ending.
    </li>
    <li>Reminders, pictures generated from the parent's themes and an image archive.</li>
    <li>
      Device job assignments, an activity log and a household service-usage limit.
    </li>
    <li>Each display has its own connection interval in Devices. It receives changes at its next connection; low-battery protection can extend the interval.</li>
    <li>The handheld camera saves photographs before starting Wi-Fi. Authenticated originals can be viewed, downloaded and deleted by the family. Offline delivery was tested on the installed camera; retries preserve the capture identifier.</li>
    <li>The camera returns a photograph of the completed sheet. The reader compares it with the original printed page; uncertain or late returns do not advance the activity. The scanner remains available.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Checks</h2>
  <p>The parent approves the initial activity. Generated activities and continuations pass format and safety checks; continuations do not require a second approval. Reading pages requires cloud connectivity. Retained data and deletion options are described under <a href="/en/#memory">memory</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="camera-checks">Camera checks</h2>
  <p>On 9 September 2026, the owner used the shutter and observed light feedback while taking battery-powered photographs. Three inspected cycles reported a confirmed preceding deep sleep, HTTP 201, matching capture and upload identifiers and an empty queue. Their preceding sleeps lasted 118, 135 and 74 seconds, measured by the device RTC at one-second resolution. These records establish those cycles, not battery life.</p>
  <p>A receiver-offline USB test kept the photograph locally and delivered the same identifier after the receiver restarted. On 10 September, a USB capture with automatic exposure, gain and white balance produced a JPEG at 1600 × 1200 pixels. The selected frame was ready in 831 ms; acquisition and verified storage took 2,307 ms. Delivery returned HTTP 201 and emptied the queue. These timings exclude boot and physical button handling, and one scene does not establish performance across lighting conditions.</p>
  <p><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/firmware/camera/README.md`}>Firmware, test conditions and diagnostic fields.</a></p>

  <h2>Open implementation gaps</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <b>Camera trials.</b> The sheet-return path has automated tests. A complete activity with photographed handwriting, varied lighting, power-interruption tests and battery-life measurements remain open. The battery cycles above concern the 9 September assembly; subsequent firmware and wiring revisions need their own physical acceptance.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>The button panel.</b> The current hardware has one button per display. It closes the paper
      loop but cannot yet capture an answer with several choices.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Memory visibility.</b> A complete view is missing. The system stores profile observations and activity summaries. Administrator development permission lasts 14 days; each permitted reading expires 14 days after its own write.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Activity quality.</b> Building, drawing and investigating can have open outcomes. Checks do not establish comprehension or interest; automatic judges retain false positives. A trial with a person is still needed.
    </li>
    <li><b>Print failure and moment timing.</b> A failed print shows a message already written in the activity, but the alternative path without a sheet is not executed. Consecutive non-collection moments advance without waiting their declared duration.</li>
    <li>
      <b>Other homes.</b> A complete installation has been tried in only one home.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/ILLUSTRATED.md`}>The system in photographs, page by page</a> ·
    <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/ideas`}>what is not built, ranked, each with a cost</a> ·
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/NON-GOALS.md`}>the lines this project will not cross</a>
  </p>
</Base>
